# Golden trace (a) "fast fills": DashDrama 1.0.6 on a device, one first-open run,
# LFO -> onboarding pager (Style5, variant 7) -> Favorite.
#
# Source: DashDrama_quickdrama_1.0.6_device/analysis/ads_events_all_runs.txt, the run of pid 31682
# (logcat 10-14 01:32:42 to 01:36:42), log lines 30-81: every NativeLanguage1/2 and NativeOnboard1-4
# LOADING/LOADED/ERROR/IMPRESSION line, plus the SplashFlow lines that name the screen action between
# them. Left out on purpose: the splash natives (NativeSplash, NativeFullSplash; DD keeps them out of
# the pool) and the interstitial / app-open lines. This run shows no NativeFull* page native of its own.
#
# Ad unit ids are replaced by their tier index inside each placement: t0 is the first id DD requested
# for that placement, t1 the second. No ad unit id appears in this file.
#
# Keys: NativeLanguage1 -> language1, NativeLanguage2 -> language2, NativeOnboard4 -> onboard4 (Style5
# page 0), NativeOnboard3 -> onboard3 (Style5 page 2, the full page; pages 1 and 3 have no native in
# variant 7, so page 1 only preloads page 2), NativeOnboard1 -> onboard1 (Favorite ad1),
# NativeOnboard2 -> onboard2 (Favorite ad2).
#
# Line format: <hh:mm:ss.SSS> <verb> <args...> [@<log line>]
#   placement <key> <ids...>            the waterfall every request for <key> carries
#   claim <key> POLITE|FORCED <result>  a screen load; the screen becomes owner when the result reports success
#   preload <key> <result>              POLITE load, owner unchanged
#   refresh <key> true|false            D-REFRESH; the value is what refresh() returns
#   set_owner <key> | clear_owner <key> owner changes on resume / onDestroyView
#   request <key> <tier>                the pool asked the loader for that tier (a LOADING line)
#   fail <key> <tier>                   that attempt failed (an ERROR line)
#   fill <key> <tier>                   that attempt filled (a LOADED line)
#   impression <key>                    the slot on screen renders <key>'s ad and reports its impression
#   select <key>|shimmer|hidden         what the selector gives here; not logged, implied by its rules
# <result> is one of requested, noop, gate_skip, transient_skip, config_skip.
# A line with @N replays log line N. A line without it is a call the SDK screens make around it that
# DD does not log (owner changes, onResume refresh and polite claim); none of them may add a request.

placement language1 t0 t1
placement language2 t0 t1
placement onboard4 t0 t1
placement onboard3 t0 t1
placement onboard1 t0 t1
placement onboard2 t0 t1

# LFO opens: polite claim of language1, then onResume refreshes (nothing held) and claims again.
01:33:26.247 claim language1 POLITE requested @31
01:33:26.247 request language1 t0 @30
01:33:26.247 select shimmer
01:33:26.258 refresh language1 false
01:33:26.258 claim language1 POLITE gate_skip @32
01:33:27.552 fail language1 t0 @34
01:33:27.567 request language1 t1 @35
01:33:29.356 fill language1 t1 @36
01:33:29.420 impression language1 @37

# First language tap: forced language2; the slot keeps borrowing the shown language1 ad.
01:33:58.564 claim language2 FORCED requested @40
01:33:58.564 request language2 t0 @39
01:33:58.564 select language1
01:34:02.135 fail language2 t0 @41
01:34:02.155 request language2 t1 @42
01:34:03.797 fill language2 t1 @43
01:34:03.830 impression language2 @44

# Second tap: language2 already holds an ad, so nothing is requested.
01:34:28.961 claim language2 FORCED noop @46

# Done: polite preload of page 0's native, then the pager replaces the LFO.
01:34:32.162 preload onboard4 requested
01:34:32.162 request onboard4 t0 @49
01:34:32.239 clear_owner language2
01:34:32.239 claim onboard4 POLITE gate_skip @50
01:34:32.243 select language2
01:34:33.873 fail onboard4 t0 @52
01:34:33.888 request onboard4 t1 @53
01:34:35.313 fill onboard4 t1 @54
01:34:35.363 impression onboard4 @55

# Page 1 has no native: it only preloads page 2's; page 0's owner keeps its ad.
01:35:08.975 preload onboard3 requested @56
01:35:08.996 request onboard3 t0 @57
01:35:08.996 select onboard4
01:35:09.814 fail onboard3 t0 @59
01:35:09.833 request onboard3 t1 @60
01:35:10.895 fill onboard3 t1 @61
01:35:10.895 select onboard4

# Page 2 (full page) claims the ad it preloaded and shows it.
01:35:24.401 claim onboard3 POLITE noop @62
01:35:24.653 impression onboard3 @64

# Page 3 has no native either.
01:35:34.418 select onboard3 @66

# Favorite: ad1 polite on view created, onResume set_owner/refresh/claim, ad2 forced on the tap.
01:35:59.340 clear_owner onboard3 @68
01:35:59.364 claim onboard1 POLITE requested
01:35:59.364 request onboard1 t0 @69
01:35:59.364 select onboard3
01:35:59.364 set_owner onboard1
01:35:59.364 refresh onboard1 false
01:35:59.364 claim onboard1 POLITE gate_skip
01:36:01.017 fail onboard1 t0 @70
01:36:01.033 request onboard1 t1 @71
01:36:02.015 fill onboard1 t1 @72
01:36:02.106 impression onboard1 @73
01:36:22.069 claim onboard2 FORCED requested @74
01:36:22.088 request onboard2 t0 @75
01:36:22.088 select onboard1
01:36:23.652 fail onboard2 t0 @76
01:36:23.668 request onboard2 t1 @77
01:36:25.160 fill onboard2 t1 @78
01:36:25.211 impression onboard2 @79

# Favorite -> Main: the owner is cleared, the leftovers stay for the resume screen.
01:36:42.851 clear_owner onboard2 @81
01:36:42.851 select onboard2
